+// A job's follow-up (semi-Markov, Dinkelbach): ending a job at group g leaves us there, and the best
+// next job h from g, worth W_h over r_gh = max(d(g, h), wait_h) + c_h rounds, is worth W_h / (1 + r_gh / H)
+// less what our best rate from here, ρ, earns over those rounds. Its excess over 0 is δ_g; ρ makes it 0
+// from here, so it prices only where a job leaves us. W_h is the worth without home weight,
+// stickiness or carry; c_h the capture and our fastest clear. The term falls in r, so Δ, its most at
+// the least rounds wait_h + c_h, bounds every δ. Read after farm's loop, for the jobs it valued
+// only. By group (padded to 4 lanes): the map's columns once read, then the turn's (begin).
+struct FollowUp {
